      "role": "user",
      "content": "the management's response was basically just \"it's part of the building's efficiency profile.\" but it feels way more intentional than that. it's almost like it's designed to keep everyone in a state of high alert or something. since it's a sub-audible frequency, i'm having trouble even finding it with my gear. are there any specific ways to shield a room from low-frequency electromagnetic or acoustic interference? like, i need to know if there's anything i can do to dampen these specific pulses in my living space.",
